# LESS Overriding & Extending Styles in Magento 2

## Table of Contents
- [1. Overview & Strategy Summary](#1-overview--strategy-summary)
- [2. The Two Core Strategies](#2-the-two-core-strategies)
  - [2.1 Override Strategy (File Copy)](#21-override-strategy-file-copy)
  - [2.2 Extension Strategy (_extend.less)](#22-extension-strategy-_extendless)
- [3. @magento_import & Import Order](#3-magento_import--import-order)
- [4. Variable Override Pattern](#4-variable-override-pattern)
- [5. Magento UI Library Mixins](#5-magento-ui-library-mixins)
  - [5.1 .lib-button()](#51-lib-button)
  - [5.2 .lib-css()](#52-lib-css)
  - [5.3 .lib-font-size()](#53-lib-font-size)
  - [5.4 .lib-line-height()](#54-lib-line-height)
  - [5.5 .lib-vendor-prefix-display()](#55-lib-vendor-prefix-display)
- [6. Media Query Mixins](#6-media-query-mixins)
- [7. Blank Theme Variables Reference](#7-blank-theme-variables-reference)
- [8. Hands-On: Button Background via _extend.less](#8-hands-on-button-background-via-_extendless)
- [9. Upgrade Safety & Best Practices](#9-upgrade-safety--best-practices)
- [10. Quick-Reference Checklist](#10-quick-reference-checklist)

---

## 1. Overview & Strategy Summary

Magento 2 uses **LESS** as its CSS pre-processor. All UI library source files live under `lib/web/css/source/lib/`. Your custom theme sits in `app/design/frontend/<Vendor>/<theme>/`. There are **two fundamentally different ways** to customise styles:

| Approach | File Location | Risk Level | Recommended? |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Override** (copy file) | Same relative path in your theme | High — you own all content | Last resort |
| **Variable override** | `web/css/source/_theme.less` in theme | Low — propagates everywhere | Preferred |
| **Extend** (_extend.less) | Alongside any source file in theme | Low — additive only | Preferred |

> **Corrected:** Variable overrides go in `_theme.less`, not `_variables.less`. The `_theme.less` file is imported in styles-m.less AFTER module styles, and its own comment says: "Theme file should contain declarations (overrides) ONLY OF EXISTING variables."

**Exam focus:**
- Overriding a file means copying it to the **exact same relative path** inside your theme.
- `_extend.less` is purely **additive** — it does not replace any core content.
- Variable overrides in `_theme.less` propagate to **every** place the variable is referenced.

---

## 2. The Two Core Strategies

### 2.1 Override Strategy (File Copy)

**When to use:** You must change logic inside a LESS file that cannot be controlled by variables or a simple extension rule.

**How it works:**

1. Locate the source file in the module or `lib/web/`.
2. Copy it to your theme at the **identical relative path**.
3. Edit the copy in your theme.

#### Example — Overriding a Module LESS File

Source file location:
```
vendor/magento/module-catalog/view/frontend/web/css/source/_module.less
```

Your override destination:
```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/Magento_Catalog/web/css/source/_module.less
```

#### Example — Overriding a lib/web File

Source:
```
lib/web/css/source/lib/_buttons.less
```

Override destination in theme:
```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/web/css/source/lib/_buttons.less
```

**File path resolution diagram:**

```
Magento resolves files in this priority order:
+------------------------------------------+
|  1. Current Theme                        |  <-- highest priority
+------------------------------------------+
         |
         v
+------------------------------------------+
|  2. Parent Theme(s) (chain upward)       |
+------------------------------------------+
         |
         v
+------------------------------------------+
|  3. Module view/frontend/web/css/source/ |
+------------------------------------------+
         |
         v
+------------------------------------------+
|  4. lib/web/css/source/                  |  <-- lowest priority
+------------------------------------------+
```

**Exam focus:**
- The override file must be at the **exact** relative path — no path shortcutting allowed.
- Module overrides go under `<theme>/<Namespace>_<Module>/web/css/source/`.
- `lib/web` overrides go under `<theme>/web/` (no module prefix).

#### The Critical Danger of Overrides

```
Core upgrade changes _buttons.less in lib/web
        |
        v
  Your override file is NOT updated
        |
        v
  Bug fixes / new features silently lost
```

> **You own 100% of the file's content from the moment you copy it.**

---

### 2.2 Extension Strategy (_extend.less)

**When to use:** You want to add new rules, override specific selectors, or call mixins with different parameters — without copying any file.

**Naming convention:** The extension file is always named `_extend.less`.

**How it works:**
Magento automatically looks for `_extend.less` files via the `@magento_import '_extend.less'` directive in styles-m.less. They are imported **after** module styles, so rules inside `_extend.less` cascade on top.

#### _extend.less Location Rules

| What you are extending | Where to place _extend.less |
|---|---|
| A module's `_module.less` | `<theme>/<Namespace>_<Module>/web/css/source/_extend.less` |
| The global theme styles | `<theme>/web/css/source/_extend.less` |

> **Corrected:** There is no `_theme_extend.less` special case. The `_extend.less` mechanism works for module scopes and the global theme scope only. To override `_theme.less` behaviour, simply redefine the variables in your own theme's `_theme.less`.

#### Example — Global _extend.less

```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/web/css/source/_extend.less
```

```less
// _extend.less — global theme extension
// Re-style the primary button using the library mixin
.action.primary {
    .lib-button(
        @_button-background: @color-blue1,
        @_button-background-hover: darken(@color-blue1, 10%)
    );
}
```

**Exam focus:**
- `_extend.less` is automatically discovered via `@magento_import` — you do **not** need to manually `@import` it.
- It is imported **after** module source files, guaranteeing higher cascade specificity.
- Module `_extend.less` files are processed **after** the module's own `_module.less`.

---

## 3. @magento_import & Import Order

Magento uses a custom preprocessor directive `@magento_import` (with **underscore**, not hyphen — not standard LESS `@import`).

> **Corrected:** The directive is `@magento_import` (underscore). Using a hyphen (`@magento-import`) will silently fail — LESS treats it as unknown syntax and ignores it.

### How @magento_import Works

```less
// Inside styles-m.less (actual content):
//@magento_import 'source/_module.less'; // Theme modules
//@magento_import 'source/_widgets.less'; // Theme widgets
```

- `@magento_import` resolves files across the **fallback chain** (theme → parent theme → module → lib).
- The `(reference)` flag is used in email-related LESS files (e.g., `@magento_import (reference) 'source/_email.less'`) to import variables/mixins without generating CSS output. It is **not** used in styles-m.less.

### Actual Import Processing Order (styles-m.less)

```
styles-m.less
    |
    +--- @import 'source/_reset.less'           (CSS reset)
    |
    +--- @import '_styles.less'                  (lib + theme sources)
    |        |
    |        +--- @import 'source/lib/_lib.less' (ALL lib mixins + variables)
    |        |
    |        +--- @import 'source/_sources.less' (theme-level components)
    |        |        |
    |        |        +--- @import '_variables.less'  (theme variable definitions)
    |        |        +--- @import (reference) '_extends.less'
    |        |        +--- @import '_typography.less', '_layout.less', ...
    |        |
    |        +--- @import 'source/_components.less'
    |
    +--- @magento_import 'source/_module.less'   (per-module styles)
    +--- @magento_import 'source/_widgets.less'  (per-module widgets)
    |
    +--- @import 'source/_theme.less'            (variable OVERRIDES — wins over all above)
    |
    +--- @magento_import 'source/_extend.less'   (additive extensions — LAST)
    |
    +--- @import 'source/lib/_responsive.less'   (media query collector)
```

> **Corrected:** The import chain is more complex than a flat list. `_styles.less` (in the blank theme) imports `_lib.less` (all library mixins/variables), then `_sources.less` (theme components including `_variables.less`). The critical point is that `_theme.less` is imported AFTER module styles, making it the correct place for variable overrides.

**Exam focus:**
- `_theme.less` is imported **after** module files — this is why theme variable overrides win.
- `@magento_import` ≠ `@import` — it understands the theme fallback chain.
- `_theme.less` is imported as a regular `@import`, not via `@magento_import`.

---

## 4. Variable Override Pattern

This is the **safest and most upgrade-friendly** customisation method.

### How Variables Propagate

```
lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_buttons.less
    defines: @button__background: @color-gray95;
                  |
                  v
    Used in: .lib-button() mixin (via .lib-css())
                  |
                  v
    Every button on the site inherits this value
```

When you redefine the variable in your theme's `_theme.less`, it overrides the lib default **everywhere** simultaneously.

### File Structure

```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/
    web/
        css/
            source/
                _theme.less      <-- YOUR variable overrides go here
```

> **Corrected:** The override file is `_theme.less`, not `_variables.less`. The blank theme's `_theme.less` comment says: "Theme file should contain declarations (overrides) ONLY OF EXISTING variables." Because `_theme.less` is imported in styles-m.less AFTER all module styles and the lib variables, your overrides are guaranteed to win.

### Example — Overriding Variables

```less
// app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/web/css/source/_theme.less

//  ============================================================
//  Colour palette overrides
//  ============================================================
@primary__color           : #1a3c5e;     // Override primary colour (lib default: @color-gray20 = #333)
@link__color              : #0066cc;     // Override link colour (lib default: @theme__color__primary = #1979c3)
@link__hover__color       : #004499;

//  ============================================================
//  Button overrides
//  ============================================================
@button__background       : @primary__color;
@button__hover__background: darken(@primary__color, 10%);
@button__color            : #ffffff;
@button__border           : 1px solid @primary__color;

//  ============================================================
//  Typography overrides
//  ============================================================
@font-size__base          : 15px;
@font-family__base        : 'Roboto', @font-family__sans-serif;

//  ============================================================
//  Header overrides
//  ============================================================
@header__background-color : @primary__color;
```

> **Corrected:** Button state variables use `@component__state__property` naming, e.g., `@button__hover__background` (NOT `@button__background-hover`). This is the consistent pattern throughout Magento's variable system.

**Exam focus:**
- Your `_theme.less` is imported **after** lib and module styles, so your values win.
- You do **not** need to copy the entire variables file — only redefine what you need.
- Variable changes affect **all** components using that variable simultaneously — one change, global effect.

### Variable Naming Convention

```
@{component}__{property}:                base value
@{component}__{state}__{property}:       state variant

Examples:
@button__background                      (base background)
@button__hover__background               (hover state background)
@button__active__background              (active state background)
@button__color                           (base text color)
@button__border-radius                   (no state — always the same)

Primary button:
@button-primary__background
@button-primary__hover__background
@button-primary__active__color
```

> **Corrected:** The naming pattern for stateful variables is `@component__state__property` (state between double-underscore separators), NOT `@component__property-state`. This matches the actual variable definitions in `lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_buttons.less`.

---

## 5. Magento UI Library Mixins

All UI library mixins are defined in `lib/web/css/source/lib/`. They follow the convention `.lib-{name}()`.

### 5.1 .lib-button()

The primary mixin for rendering styled buttons. It outputs all button-related CSS properties from its parameters.

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_buttons.less`

#### Signature (key parameters)

```less
.lib-button(
    @_button-font-family        : @button__font-family,
    @_button-font-size          : @button__font-size,
    @_button-font-weight        : @button__font-weight,
    @_button-cursor             : @button__cursor,
    @_button-display            : @button__display,
    @_button-disabled-opacity   : @button__disabled__opacity,
    @_button-line-height        : @button__line-height,
    @_button-width              : @button__width,
    @_button-margin             : @button__margin,
    @_button-padding            : @button__padding,

    // Colour (text)
    @_button-color              : @button__color,
    // Background
    @_button-background         : @button__background,
    // Border
    @_button-border             : @button__border,

    // Hover state
    @_button-color-hover        : @button__hover__color,
    @_button-background-hover   : @button__hover__background,
    @_button-border-hover       : @button__hover__border,

    // Active state
    @_button-color-active       : @button__active__color,
    @_button-background-active  : @button__active__background,
    @_button-border-active      : @button__active__border,

    // Gradient (all false by default)
    @_button-gradient           : @button__gradient,
    @_button-gradient-direction : @button__gradient-direction,
    // ... gradient color stops ...

    // Icon parameters
    @_button-icon-use           : @button-icon__use,
    // ... icon font properties ...
);
```

> **Corrected:** The mixin parameter defaults reference the actual variable names, e.g., `@button__hover__color` (state between component and property), not `@button__color-hover`. The full mixin has ~30+ parameters including gradient and icon support.

#### Usage Example in _extend.less

```less
// Override the primary action button background colour
.action.primary {
    .lib-button(
        @_button-background       : #1a6faf,
        @_button-background-hover : #145989,
        @_button-background-active: #0f4268,
        @_button-color            : #ffffff,
        @_button-border           : 1px solid #1a6faf,
        @_button-border-hover     : 1px solid #145989
    );
}

// Override ALL primary buttons site-wide (via variable)
// Place in _theme.less instead for global effect:
// @button-primary__background: #1a6faf;
```

**Exam focus:**
- `.lib-button()` accepts named parameters — only supply the ones you want to override.
- Parameters follow `@_button-` prefix convention.
- Prefer variable overrides (in `_theme.less`) over passing individual mixin parameters when the change should be global.
- `.lib-button-l()` and `.lib-button-s()` exist for large/small button size variants.

---

### 5.2 .lib-css()

A utility mixin that outputs a CSS property **only if the value is not `false`**. This is Magento's mechanism for conditional CSS output.

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_utilities.less`

#### Signature

```less
.lib-css(
    @_property,   // CSS property name (e.g., color, font-size)
    @_value,      // value to apply
    @_prefix: 0   // optional: add vendor prefixes (1 = yes)
);
```

#### Usage Examples

```less
// Basic usage — outputs: color: #ff0000;
.lib-css(color, #ff0000);

// Value is false — outputs NOTHING (no CSS property emitted)
.lib-css(color, false);

// With vendor prefix (@_prefix: 1)
.lib-css(transform, rotate(45deg), 1);
// Outputs:
//   -webkit-transform: rotate(45deg);
//   -moz-transform: rotate(45deg);
//   -ms-transform: rotate(45deg);
//   transform: rotate(45deg);
```

> **Corrected:** When `@_prefix = 1`, the mixin outputs `-webkit-`, `-moz-`, and `-ms-` prefixed versions PLUS the standard property. The original notes omitted the `-moz-` prefix.

#### Practical pattern — conditional overrides

```less
// In your _theme.less:
@my-custom-border-radius : false;  // Set to false to disable, or a value to enable

// In a mixin or rule:
.my-widget {
    .lib-css(border-radius, @my-custom-border-radius);
    // If false: no border-radius output
    // If '5px': outputs border-radius: 5px;
}
```

**Exam focus:**
- `.lib-css()` outputs **nothing** when the value is `false` — this is how Magento makes variables optional.
- This is why you see `@variable: false` in variable files for "disabled by default" features.
- Multi-value properties (e.g., shorthand) are also suppressed if ANY component is `false`.

---

### 5.3 .lib-font-size()

Sets `font-size` with automatic unit conversion based on the configured `@font-size-unit` (default: `rem`).

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_typography.less`

#### Signature

```less
.lib-font-size(
    @sizeValue   // accepts a value; converts to @font-size-unit (default: rem)
);
```

#### Usage Example

```less
.page-title {
    .lib-font-size(32);
}

// Output (with default settings: @font-size-unit = rem, @font-size-unit-ratio = 10):
// .page-title {
//     font-size: 3.2rem;    /* 32 / 10 = 3.2rem */
// }
```

> **Corrected:** `.lib-font-size()` does NOT output dual px + rem values. It converts the input to the configured `@font-size-unit` (default: `rem`) using `@font-size-unit-ratio`. With default settings, `@font-size-unit-ratio` = 10 (derived from `@root__font-size: 62.5%` × 16 / 100), so an input of 32 outputs `3.2rem`, not `2rem`. If `@font-size-unit-convert` is `false`, the raw value is output unchanged.

**Exam focus:**
- Input is typically in **pixels** (can be unitless integer).
- Output is in the configured `@font-size-unit` (default: `rem`).
- `@root__font-size` is `62.5%` (not `10px`) — this makes 1rem = 10px (62.5% of browser's 16px default).
- The conversion ratio is `@font-size-unit-ratio: 10`, so divide by 10 to get rem value.

---

### 5.4 .lib-line-height()

Sets `line-height` using the same unit conversion approach as `.lib-font-size()`.

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_typography.less`

#### Signature

```less
.lib-line-height(
    @heightValue   // value to convert; also accepts percentages and 'normal'
);
```

#### Usage Example

```less
.product-name {
    .lib-font-size(18);
    .lib-line-height(28);
}

// Output (with default settings):
// .product-name {
//     font-size: 1.8rem;
//     line-height: 2.8rem;
// }
```

---

### 5.5 .lib-vendor-prefix-display()

Outputs `display` with all required vendor prefixes, primarily for Flexbox support.

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_utilities.less`

#### Signature

```less
.lib-vendor-prefix-display(
    @_value: flex   // flex | inline-flex | block | etc.
);
```

#### Usage Example

```less
.my-flex-container {
    .lib-vendor-prefix-display(flex);
}

// Output:
// .my-flex-container {
//     display: -webkit-flex;
//     display: -ms-flexbox;
//     display: flex;
// }
```

> **Note:** The `-ms-` prefix appends `box` to the value (e.g., `flex` → `-ms-flexbox`, `inline-flex` → `-ms-inline-flexbox`), while `-webkit-` preserves the value as-is.

**Exam focus:**
- Use `.lib-vendor-prefix-display()` instead of writing `display: flex` directly — ensures cross-browser compatibility within Magento's framework pattern.
- The mixin handles the IE11 Flexbox naming difference (`-ms-flexbox` instead of `-ms-flex`).

---

## 6. Media Query Mixins

### .media-width(@extremum, @break)

Magento provides a standardised media query mixin pattern to ensure consistent responsive breakpoints across all modules and themes.

**Location:** `lib/web/css/source/lib/_responsive.less`

#### How It Works

The `.media-width()` pattern uses LESS mixin guards. You DEFINE a mixin with specific guard conditions, and `_responsive.less` CALLS those definitions inside the correct `@media` blocks:

```less
// Your definition (in _module.less or _extend.less):
.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'min') and (@break = @screen__m) {
    .my-element {
        display: flex;
        padding: 20px;
    }
}

// _responsive.less calls it inside:
// @media all and (min-width: 768px) { .media-width('min', @screen__m); }
```

> **Corrected:** The actual codebase uses the guard syntax `when (@extremum = 'min') and (@break = @screen__m)`. While the shorthand syntax `.media-width('min', @screen__m) { ... }` also works in LESS, the guard syntax is the convention used throughout the Magento codebase.

#### Standard Breakpoint Variables

| Variable | Default Value | Typical Use |
|---|---|---|
| `@screen__xxs` | 320px | Tiny phones |
| `@screen__xs` | 480px | Small phones |
| `@screen__s` | 640px | Large phones |
| `@screen__m` | 768px | Tablets (main mobile/desktop split) |
| `@screen__l` | 1024px | Laptops / small desktops |
| `@screen__xl` | 1440px | Large desktops |

#### Usage Examples

```less
// Mobile-first: applies from 768px and UP
.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'min') and (@break = @screen__m) {
    .my-element {
        display: flex;
        padding: 20px;
    }
}

// Desktop-first: applies up to 767px (max-width)
.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'max') and (@break = @screen__m) {
    .my-element {
        display: block;
        padding: 10px;
    }
}
```

#### Compiled Output

```css
/* 'min', @screen__m compiles to: */
@media all and (min-width: 768px) {
    .my-element {
        display: flex;
        padding: 20px;
    }
}

/* 'max', @screen__m compiles to: */
@media only screen and (max-width: 767px) {
    .my-element {
        display: block;
        padding: 10px;
    }
}
```

> **Note:** When using `max`, `_responsive.less` subtracts 1px from the breakpoint value to avoid overlap (e.g., `@screen__m` = 768px → `max-width: 767px`). The `min` media queries use `@media all and`, while `max` queries use `@media only screen and`.

**Exam focus:**
- The mixin uses guard syntax with `@extremum` (`'min'` or `'max'`) and `@break` (breakpoint variable).
- `max` breakpoints subtract 1px from the variable value automatically.
- You can override breakpoint variables in your theme's `_theme.less` to change all responsive behaviour globally.
- `_responsive.less` must be imported LAST (it is, at the end of styles-m.less) so that all `.media-width()` definitions are collected before being output.

---

## 7. Blank Theme Variables Reference

The Magento Blank theme (`Magento/blank`) is the **recommended base** for all custom themes. Variables are defined across multiple files in `lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/`, with the Blank theme overriding some in its own `web/css/source/_variables.less`.

> **Corrected:** The notes originally said variables are in `lib/web/css/source/_variables.less` — that file is actually EMPTY (its comment says "Should be EMPTY"). The real variable definitions live in `lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_colors.less`, `_typography.less`, `_buttons.less`, `_layout.less`, etc.

### Key Variable Groups

#### Colour Palette

```less
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_colors.less

//  Base colours
@color-black                    : #000;
@color-white                    : #fff;
@color-red10                    : #e02b27;  // error red
@color-orange-red1              : #ff5501;  // secondary/accent colour
@color-blue1                    : #1979c3;  // primary theme colour
@color-blue2                    : #006bb4;  // primary alt (hover)

//  Colour nesting (semantic aliases)
@theme__color__primary          : @color-blue1;
@theme__color__primary-alt      : @color-blue2;
@theme__color__secondary        : @color-orange-red1;

@primary__color                 : @color-gray20;        // #333 — main text colour
@secondary__color               : @color-gray91;        // #e8e8e8
@page__background-color         : @color-white;
@active__color                  : @theme__color__secondary;
@error__color                   : @color-red10;         // #e02b27
```

> **Corrected:** `@primary__color` is `@color-gray20` (#333), NOT `@color-brownie`. `@secondary__color` is `@color-gray91`, NOT `@color-white-fog`. `@color-orange-red1` is `#ff5501`, NOT `#e02b27` (that's `@color-red10`). `@sidebar__background-color` is defined in the Blank theme's `_variables.less` as `@color-white-smoke` (#f5f5f5).

#### Typography

```less
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_typography.less

@font-family__sans-serif        : 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
@font-family__monospace         : Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace;
@font-family__base              : @font-family__sans-serif; // Blank theme overrides to include Open Sans

// Blank theme override (vendor/magento/theme-frontend-blank/web/css/source/_variables.less):
// @font-family-name__base: 'Open Sans';
// @font-family__base: @font-family-name__base, @font-family__sans-serif;
// Result: 'Open Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif

@root__font-size                : 62.5%;  // NOT 10px — 62.5% of 16px browser default = 10px
@font-size__base                : 14px;   // Computed from @root__font-size and @font-size-ratio__base
@font-size__xl                  : ceil(1.5 * @font-size__base);  // 21px
@font-size__l                   : ceil(1.25 * @font-size__base); // 18px
@font-size__s                   : ceil(.85 * @font-size__base);  // 12px
@font-size__xs                  : floor(.75 * @font-size__base); // 11px

@font-weight__light             : 300;
@font-weight__regular           : 400;
@font-weight__heavier           : 500;
@font-weight__semibold          : 600;
@font-weight__bold              : 700;

@line-height__base              : 1.428571429;
@line-height__computed          : floor(@font-size__base * @line-height__base); // 20px
```

#### Layout & Spacing

```less
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_typography.less (indents)
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_layout.less (layout)

@indent__base                   : @line-height__computed; // 20px (NOT @font-size__base * 2)
@indent__xl                     : @indent__base * 2;      // 40px
@indent__l                      : @indent__base * 1.5;    // 30px
@indent__m                      : @indent__base * 1.25;   // 25px
@indent__s                      : (@indent__base / 2);    // 10px
@indent__xs                     : (@indent__base / 4);    // 5px

@layout__max-width              : 1280px;
@total-columns                  : 12;
@layout-column__sidebar-width   : 2;  // 2 out of 12 columns (NOT 6/12)
```

> **Corrected:** `@indent__base` is `@line-height__computed` (20px), NOT `@font-size__base * 2` (28px). This changes ALL indent calculations. `@layout-column__sidebar-width` is `2` (2/12 grid columns), not `6/12`. There is no `@layout__min-width` variable.

#### Button Variables

```less
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_buttons.less

//  Default (secondary) button
@button__font-size              : @font-size__base;      // 14px
@button__font-weight            : @font-weight__bold;    // 700 (NOT semibold/600)
@button__line-height            : @font-size__base + 2;  // 16 (unitless)
@button__padding                : 7px 15px;              // Shorthand (NOT separate top/right/bottom/left)
@button__background             : @color-gray95;         // #f2f2f2 (NOT brownie)
@button__color                  : @primary__color;       // #333 (NOT white)
@button__border                 : 1px solid @color-gray-darken2; // #cdcdcd
@button__border-radius          : 3px;
@button__cursor                 : pointer;
@button__display                : inline-block;

@button__hover__background      : @color-gray-darken1;   // #e2e2e2
@button__hover__color           : @color-gray-darken3;   // #555
@button__active__background     : @button__hover__background;
@button__active__color          : @button__color;

//  Primary button
@button-primary__background     : @theme__color__primary;      // @color-blue1 = #1979c3
@button-primary__border         : 1px solid @theme__color__primary;
@button-primary__color          : @color-white;

@button-primary__hover__background : @theme__color__primary-alt; // @color-blue2 = #006bb4
@button-primary__hover__border  : 1px solid @theme__color__primary-alt;
@button-primary__hover__color   : @button-primary__color;

@button-primary__active__background : @button-primary__hover__background;
```

> **Corrected:** Nearly all button variable values in the original notes were fabricated. Key fixes: `@button__font-weight` is `@font-weight__bold` (700), NOT `@font-weight__semibold` (600). `@button__background` is `@color-gray95` (#f2f2f2), NOT `@color-brownie1`. `@button__color` is `@primary__color` (#333), NOT white. `@button-primary__background` is `@theme__color__primary` (#1979c3), NOT `@color-orange-red1`. State variables use `__state__` naming: `@button__hover__background`, `@button-primary__hover__border`, etc.

#### Link Variables

```less
// lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/_typography.less

@link__color                    : @theme__color__primary;      // @color-blue1 = #1979c3
@link__text-decoration          : none;
@link__visited__color           : @link__color;
@link__visited__text-decoration : none;
@link__hover__color             : @theme__color__primary-alt;  // @color-blue2 = #006bb4
@link__hover__text-decoration   : underline;
@link__active__color            : @active__color;              // @color-orange-red1 = #ff5501
@link__active__text-decoration  : underline;
```

> **Corrected:** `@link__color` is `@theme__color__primary` (NOT `@theme__color__primary-darker` — that variable doesn't exist). `@link__hover__color` is `@theme__color__primary-alt` (NOT `@theme__color__primary-darker`).

**Exam focus:**
- Variables are spread across `lib/web/css/source/lib/variables/` — each component has its own file.
- All variables use the `@component__property` or `@component__state__property` naming pattern.
- `false` as a value means "don't output this property" (used with `.lib-css()`).
- You should extend Blank theme (`Magento/blank`) as your parent — never modify lib directly.

---

## 8. Hands-On: Button Background via _extend.less

This walkthrough changes the primary button background colour using `_extend.less` and the `.lib-button()` mixin.

### Step 1 — Create the _extend.less File

```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/
    web/
        css/
            source/
                _extend.less     <-- create this file
```

### Step 2 — Option A: Use .lib-button() with Direct Parameters

```less
// app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/web/css/source/_extend.less

//  ============================================================
//  Primary Button Override — using .lib-button() mixin params
//  ============================================================

.action.primary {
    .lib-button(
        @_button-background        : #1a6faf,
        @_button-background-hover  : #145989,
        @_button-background-active : #0f4268,
        @_button-color             : #ffffff,
        @_button-border            : 1px solid #1a6faf,
        @_button-border-hover      : 1px solid #145989,
        @_button-border-radius     : 4px
    );
}
```

### Step 3 — Option B (Preferred): Override Variables in _theme.less

```less
// app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/web/css/source/_theme.less

//  Primary button colour scheme
@button-primary__background        : #1a6faf;
@button-primary__hover__background : #145989;
@button-primary__active__background: #0f4268;
@button-primary__color             : #ffffff;
@button-primary__border            : 1px solid #1a6faf;
@button-primary__hover__border     : 1px solid #145989;
```

> **Corrected:** Variable overrides go in `_theme.less` (not `_variables.less`). Variable names use `__state__` notation: `@button-primary__hover__background` (NOT `@button-primary__background-hover`), `@button-primary__hover__border` (NOT `@button-primary__hover__border` — actually this one was already correct but now uses the verified actual variable name).

Then in `_extend.less`, simply call the mixin with no overrides — the variables do all the work:

```less
// _extend.less — no mixin param overrides needed;
// variable changes propagate automatically.

// Only needed if the selector itself needs different treatment:
.action.primary {
    .lib-button-l();  // example: use large button variant (larger font + padding)
}
```

### Step 4 — Using Responsive Overrides in _extend.less

```less
// _extend.less — full responsive button example

.action.primary {
    .lib-button(
        @_button-background       : #1a6faf,
        @_button-background-hover : #145989,
        @_button-color            : #ffffff
    );
}

// Mobile: full-width buttons
.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'max') and (@break = @screen__m) {
    .action.primary {
        width: 100%;
        text-align: center;
    }
}

// Desktop: inline with larger padding
.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'min') and (@break = @screen__m) {
    .action.primary {
        .lib-css(padding-left, 30px);
        .lib-css(padding-right, 30px);
    }
}
```

> **Corrected:** `.media-width()` definitions must be at the TOP LEVEL of the file (not nested inside a selector). The mixin guard pattern requires standalone definitions that `_responsive.less` collects and outputs inside the appropriate `@media` blocks.

### Step 5 — Deploy and Verify

```bash
# Clean generated CSS
rm -rf var/view_preprocessed pub/static/frontend/

# Deploy theme source files (development)
bin/magento dev:source-theme:deploy

# OR for development mode (auto-compilation):
bin/magento deploy:mode:set developer

# Force regeneration
bin/magento setup:static-content:deploy -f en_US

# Clear cache
bin/magento cache:clean
bin/magento cache:flush
```

> **Corrected:** `dev:css:deploy` does NOT exist. The correct command is `dev:source-theme:deploy` (from module-developer).

**Exam focus:**
- `_extend.less` is auto-discovered via `@magento_import` — no `@import` statement is needed.
- Option B (variable overrides in `_theme.less`) is always preferred over Option A (mixin parameter overrides) because variable changes are globally consistent.
- Always clear `var/view_preprocessed` when LESS changes don't appear — compiled CSS is cached there.

---

## 9. Upgrade Safety & Best Practices

### The Override Risk Matrix

```
Risk Level:   LOW ---------> HIGH
              |                 |
              v                 v
        _theme.less        Copied file
        _extend.less       (lib/web or module)
              |                 |
        Upgrade safe       YOU own ALL content
        Core updates       Core updates IGNORED
        still apply        SILENTLY
```

### Decision Flow for Customising Styles

```
Need to customise a style?
          |
          v
Can it be done via a variable in _theme.less?
    YES ---> Do it there (safest)
          |
          NO
          |
          v
Can it be done by adding/overriding rules in _extend.less?
    YES ---> Use _extend.less (safe)
          |
          NO
          |
          v
Must you change the internal logic of a LESS file?
    YES ---> Copy-override (last resort, document why)
```

### Best Practice Rules

| Rule | Reason |
|---|---|
| Never edit `lib/web/css/` directly | Cannot be tracked in theme; lost on upgrade |
| Never edit `vendor/magento/*/web/css/` directly | Core file; lost on upgrade |
| Always extend `Magento/blank` as parent | Gets all lib variable definitions |
| Use `_extend.less` for additive changes | Upgrade safe; no file duplication |
| Use `_theme.less` for value changes | Global propagation; imported after modules |
| Document every file override | Future developers need to know |
| Test after every Magento upgrade | Override files need manual merge |

### File Override Audit Command

```bash
# Find all overridden LESS files in your theme
find app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme -name "*.less" | \
    grep -v "_extend.less" | \
    grep -v "_theme.less"
```

### Complete Directory Structure Example

```
app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/
|
+-- web/
|   +-- css/
|       +-- source/
|           +-- _theme.less          (variable overrides — the recommended override file)
|           +-- _extend.less         (global additive rules)
|
+-- Magento_Catalog/
|   +-- web/
|       +-- css/
|           +-- source/
|               +-- _extend.less     (catalog-specific additions)
|               +-- _module.less     (OVERRIDE — only if truly necessary)
|
+-- Magento_Checkout/
    +-- web/
        +-- css/
            +-- source/
                +-- _extend.less     (checkout-specific additions)
```

