## 10. Quick-Reference Checklist

### Core Concepts

- [ ] **Override strategy**: Copy file to **exact relative path** in your theme — you own 100% of its content from that point
- [ ] **Extension strategy**: Create `_extend.less` alongside the file being extended — purely additive, auto-discovered
- [ ] **Variable override**: Define variables in `<theme>/web/css/source/_theme.less` — propagates everywhere the variable is used
- [ ] **Import order**: `_theme.less` is imported **after** module files — guarantees theme variable overrides win
- [ ] `@magento_import` ≠ `@import` — Magento's directive (with underscore) understands the theme fallback chain
- [ ] The `(reference)` flag can be used with `@magento_import` (seen in email LESS files) to import without CSS output

### Override vs. Extend

- [ ] Overriding a file = copying it to theme at same relative path
- [ ] Module overrides live at `<theme>/<Namespace>_<Module>/web/css/source/`
- [ ] lib/web overrides live at `<theme>/web/` (same relative path, no module prefix)
- [ ] `_extend.less` is **automatically imported** via `@magento_import` in styles-m.less
- [ ] Do **not** manually `@import` your `_extend.less` file — Magento handles it

### Variable System

- [ ] Variables defined in theme `_theme.less` **override** lib defaults
- [ ] Value of `false` means "don't output this CSS property" (used with `.lib-css()`)
- [ ] Variable naming: `@component__property`, `@component__state__property` (state between component and property)
- [ ] Breakpoint variables: `@screen__xxs`, `@screen__xs`, `@screen__s`, `@screen__m`, `@screen__l`, `@screen__xl`

### UI Library Mixins

- [ ] `.lib-button()` — all button styles; named params with `@_button-` prefix
- [ ] `.lib-css(@_property, @_value)` — outputs CSS only if value is **not** `false`
- [ ] `.lib-font-size(@sizeValue)` — converts to configured `@font-size-unit` (default: `rem`)
- [ ] `.lib-line-height(@heightValue)` — converts to configured `@font-size-unit`
- [ ] `.lib-vendor-prefix-display(@_value)` — adds `-webkit-` and `-ms-` prefixes for `display`

### Media Queries

- [ ] `.media-width(@extremum, @break) when (@extremum = 'min') and (@break = @screen__m)` — guard syntax
- [ ] `'max'` breakpoints auto-subtract 1px from the variable value
- [ ] Always use **breakpoint variables**, never raw pixel values
- [ ] Override breakpoint variables in `_theme.less` to adjust all responsive behaviour globally
- [ ] `.media-width()` definitions must be at the top level of the file

### Hands-On Button Task

- [ ] Create `_extend.less` at `<theme>/web/css/source/_extend.less`
- [ ] Use `.lib-button()` with `@_button-background`, `@_button-background-hover` parameters
- [ ] **Preferred**: set `@button-primary__background` in `_theme.less` instead for global effect
- [ ] Clear `var/view_preprocessed` AND `pub/static/frontend/` after LESS changes
- [ ] Run `bin/magento setup:static-content:deploy` or use developer mode for auto-compilation

### Upgrade Safety Rules

- [ ] **NEVER** edit `lib/web/css/` or core module CSS directly
- [ ] Minimise file overrides — prefer variables and `_extend.less`
- [ ] Every copied LESS file **must** be manually checked after Magento upgrades
- [ ] Extend `Magento/blank` (not `Magento/luma`) as your theme parent for proper variable access
- [ ] Document every override file with a comment explaining why it was necessary

