## Quick-Reference Checklist

### File Locations
- [ ] Module config: `app/code/Vendor/Module/view/frontend/requirejs-config.js`
- [ ] Theme config: `app/design/frontend/Vendor/theme/requirejs-config.js`
- [ ] Variable in file **must** be named `var config = { ... }`

### Configuration Sections
- [ ] **`paths`** — maps a short alias to a file path (no `.js` extension, no absolute paths)
- [ ] **`map`** — remaps one module ID to another module ID; `"*"` applies globally
- [ ] **`shim`** — wraps non-AMD legacy libraries; use `deps` and `exports` properties
- [ ] **`deps`** — array of modules to auto-load on RequireJS initialization
- [ ] **`config > mixins`** — extends an existing module; set to `true` to enable, `false` to disable

### AMD Patterns
- [ ] `define([deps], function(dep){})` — creates a reusable module (use in `.js` files)
- [ ] `require([deps], callback)` — loads and consumes modules (use in entry points)
- [ ] Always use **anonymous** `define()` — never include a module name as first argument
- [ ] `define()` file doesn't execute until it is `require()`-d somewhere

### Module ID Resolution Fallback Order
- [ ] Theme → Parent Theme(s) → Module (`view/frontend/web/`) → `lib/web/`
- [ ] Theme file at `Vendor_Module/web/js/file.js` automatically overrides module's version

### Config Merging Rules
- [ ] ALL `requirejs-config.js` files across all enabled modules and active theme are **merged**
- [ ] Later configs (theme > module) **extend** earlier configs — not full replacements
- [ ] For `paths`: last definition of a key **wins**
- [ ] For `mixins`: all mixins for a target are **additive** — all apply

### map vs paths vs mixins
- [ ] `paths` → alias to a **file location**
- [ ] `map` → alias to a **different module ID** (for substitution/replacement)
- [ ] `mixins` → **extend** an existing module non-destructively

### Common Mistakes to Avoid
- [ ] Never use absolute paths (`/pub/static/...`) in `paths` config
- [ ] Never include `.js` extension in module IDs or `paths` values
- [ ] Never shim a library that already uses AMD `define()`
- [ ] Never assume one `requirejs-config.js` overrides another — they merge
- [ ] Never use named `define('module/id', ...)` in Magento module files

### Browser Debugging Commands
- [ ] `require.s.contexts._.config.paths` — inspect all registered path aliases
- [ ] `require.s.contexts._.defined` — inspect all loaded module definitions
- [ ] `require(['myAlias'], function(m){ console.log(m); })` — test-load a module by alias

