### 3.4 XML Configuration Deep-Dive

UI Component XML files live in `view/adminhtml/ui_component/` (admin) or `view/frontend/ui_component/` (frontend).

```xml
<!-- File: app/code/Vendor/Module/view/adminhtml/ui_component/vendor_module_entity_listing.xml -->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<listing xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Ui:etc/ui_configuration.xsd">

    <!-- Argument section: component configuration -->
    <argument name="data" xsi:type="array">
        <item name="js_config" xsi:type="array">
            <!-- Provider: the data source for this component -->
            <item name="provider" xsi:type="string">
                vendor_module_entity_listing.vendor_module_entity_listing_data_source
            </item>
        </item>
    </argument>

    <!-- Settings section (newer syntax) -->
    <settings>
        <spinner>vendor_module_entity_listing_columns</spinner>
        <deps>
            <!-- Component must wait for data provider to load -->
            <dep>vendor_module_entity_listing.vendor_module_entity_listing_data_source</dep>
        </deps>
    </settings>

    <!-- Data source: connects to PHP DataProvider class -->
    <dataSource name="vendor_module_entity_listing_data_source"
                component="Magento_Ui/js/grid/provider">
        <settings>
            <storageConfig>
                <param name="indexField" xsi:type="string">entity_id</param>
            </storageConfig>
            <updateUrl path="mui/index/render"/>
        </settings>
        <aclResource>Vendor_Module::manage</aclResource>
        <dataProvider class="Vendor\Module\Ui\DataProvider\Entity\ListingDataProvider"
                      name="vendor_module_entity_listing_data_source">
            <settings>
                <requestFieldName>id</requestFieldName>
                <primaryFieldName>entity_id</primaryFieldName>
            </settings>
        </dataProvider>
    </dataSource>

    <!-- Listing toolbar: search + filters + pager -->
    <listingToolbar name="listing_top">
        <settings>
            <sticky>true</sticky>
        </settings>
        <bookmark name="bookmarks"/>
        <columnsControls name="columns_controls"/>
        <filterSearch name="fulltext"/>
        <filters name="listing_filters"/>
        <paging name="listing_paging"/>
    </listingToolbar>

    <!-- Column set -->
    <columns name="vendor_module_entity_listing_columns">
        <!-- Checkbox column for mass actions -->
        <selectionsColumn name="ids">
            <settings>
                <indexField>entity_id</indexField>
            </settings>
        </selectionsColumn>

        <!-- Regular data columns -->
        <column name="entity_id">
            <settings>
                <filter>textRange</filter>
                <label translate="true">ID</label>
                <sorting>asc</sorting>
            </settings>
        </column>

        <column name="name">
            <settings>
                <filter>text</filter>
                <label translate="true">Name</label>
            </settings>
        </column>

        <!-- Actions column -->
        <actionsColumn name="actions"
                       class="Vendor\Module\Ui\Component\Listing\Column\Actions">
            <settings>
                <indexField>entity_id</indexField>
            </settings>
        </actionsColumn>
    </columns>
</listing>
```

> **Exam focus:** The `dataSource` element's `dataProvider` `class` attribute points to a **PHP class**, while the `component` attribute of `dataSource` points to a **JS module**. These are different and serve different purposes.

---

### 3.5 Data Providers

A **data provider** is a PHP class that feeds data to a UI component via AJAX. It extends `\Magento\Ui\DataProvider\AbstractDataProvider`.

```php
<?php
// File: app/code/Vendor/Module/Ui/DataProvider/Entity/ListingDataProvider.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Ui\DataProvider\Entity;

use Magento\Ui\DataProvider\AbstractDataProvider;
use Vendor\Module\Model\ResourceModel\Entity\CollectionFactory;

class ListingDataProvider extends AbstractDataProvider
{
    /**
     * @param string $name
     * @param string $primaryFieldName
     * @param string $requestFieldName
     * @param CollectionFactory $collectionFactory
     * @param array $meta
     * @param array $data
     */
    public function __construct(
        string $name,
        string $primaryFieldName,
        string $requestFieldName,
        CollectionFactory $collectionFactory,
        array $meta = [],
        array $data = []
    ) {
        parent::__construct($name, $primaryFieldName, $requestFieldName, $meta, $data);
        // The parent stores it as $this->collection
        $this->collection = $collectionFactory->create();
    }

    /**
     * Get data for the grid
     * @return array
     */
    public function getData(): array
    {
        if (!$this->getCollection()->isLoaded()) {
            $this->getCollection()->load();
        }

        $items = $this->getCollection()->toArray();

        return [
            'totalRecords' => $this->getCollection()->getSize(),
            'items' => array_values($items['items'] ?? $items),
        ];
    }
}
```

> **Exam focus:** The data provider's `getData()` method must return an array with `totalRecords` and `items` keys for the grid to function properly.

**For admin Forms**, the data provider is similar but returns data keyed by entity ID:

```php
public function getData(): array
{
    $items = [];
    foreach ($this->getCollection() as $entity) {
        $items[$entity->getId()] = $entity->getData();
    }
    return $items;
}
```

