## 5. Common Pitfalls & Tricky Exam Scenarios

### Pitfall 1: Observable = Assignment (Critical)

```javascript
// WRONG — replaces observable with string, breaks all KO bindings
this.customerName = 'John';

// CORRECT — updates observable value, triggers UI refresh
this.customerName('John');
```

### Pitfall 2: Forgetting _super()

```javascript
// WRONG — parent initialize() never runs, checkout will break
initialize: function () {
    this.customProp('value');
    return this;
},

// CORRECT — parent logic preserved
initialize: function () {
    this._super();  // Parent runs first (or sometimes after, by design)
    this.customProp('value');
    return this;
}
```

### Pitfall 3: Mixin File Not Returning a Function

```javascript
// WRONG — returns extended component directly, not a function
define([], function () {
    return TargetModule.extend({  // TargetModule is not in scope!
        initialize: function () { ... }
    });
});

// CORRECT — returns a function that receives TargetModule
define([], function () {
    return function (TargetModule) {
        return TargetModule.extend({
            initialize: function () { ... }
        });
    };
});
```

### Pitfall 4: requirejs-config.js Nesting

```javascript
// WRONG — missing inner 'config' key
var config = {
    mixins: {  // Wrong! mixins is not a top-level key
        'Target': { 'Mixin': true }
    }
};

// CORRECT
var config = {
    config: {      // Inner 'config' is required
        mixins: {
            'Target': { 'Mixin': true }
        }
    }
};
```

### Pitfall 5: Reading $index in foreach without calling it

```html
<!-- WRONG: $index is an observable, not a plain number -->
<span data-bind="text: $index"></span>   <!-- Shows function code! -->

<!-- CORRECT: call $index() to get the numeric value -->
<span data-bind="text: $index()"></span>
```

### Pitfall 6: ko.computed() without context

```javascript
// WRONG — 'this' inside computed is window/undefined
this.fullName = ko.computed(function () {
    return this.firstName() + ' ' + this.lastName(); // 'this' is wrong!
});

// CORRECT — pass 'this' as second argument
this.fullName = ko.computed(function () {
    return this.firstName() + ' ' + this.lastName();
}, this);  // 'this' context bound correctly
```

### Pitfall 7: Modifying observableArray items vs the array itself

```javascript
var arr = this.cartItems; // arr is the observable array function

// CORRECT: mutate via observable array methods
arr.push(newItem);
arr.remove(oldItem);

// WRONG: getting the array and mutating it directly
var rawArr = this.cartItems();  // rawArr is a plain JS array
rawArr.push(newItem);  // KO doesn't know about this change!
```

> **Exam focus:** All of the above pitfalls have been seen in exam scenarios. Pay special attention to: observable get/set syntax, `_super()` in mixins, and the double-`config` nesting in `requirejs-config.js`.

---

## 6. Quick-Reference Checklist

### JavaScript Mixins

- [ ] Mixin declaration: `var config = { config: { mixins: { 'target': { 'mixin': true } } } }`
- [ ] Double `config` nesting is **required** in `requirejs-config.js`
- [ ] Mixin value: `true` enables, `false` disables
- [ ] Mixin file **must return a function** that accepts `TargetModule`
- [ ] That function **must return** the extended/modified module
- [ ] Use `TargetModule.extend({})` for class-based (uiElement) targets
- [ ] Use function wrapping for plain function targets
- [ ] Use property patching for plain object targets
- [ ] **Always call `this._super()`** in overridden methods to preserve parent behavior
- [ ] Stacked mixins receive the previous mixin's output, not the original
- [ ] Frontend mixins go in `view/frontend/requirejs-config.js`
- [ ] Admin mixins go in `view/adminhtml/requirejs-config.js`

### Knockout.js Observables

- [ ] Declare: `this.name = ko.observable('initial')`
- [ ] Get value: `this.name()` — call as function, no argument
- [ ] Set value: `this.name('newValue')` — call as function with argument
- [ ] **NEVER** use `=` assignment on an observable — it destroys it
- [ ] Observable array: `ko.observableArray([])`
- [ ] Array mutation: use `.push()`, `.pop()`, `.remove()` on the observable, not the raw array
- [ ] Get raw array: `this.myArray()`; `.length` on `this.myArray().length`
- [ ] Computed: `ko.computed(function(){ ... }, this)` — second arg is `this` context
- [ ] `ko.pureComputed()` for memory-efficient read-only computeds
- [ ] Subscribe: `this.name.subscribe(function(newVal){ ... })`

### Knockout.js Bindings

- [ ] `text:` — renders as text node (safe, escapes HTML)
- [ ] `html:` — renders as HTML (XSS risk)
- [ ] `value:` — two-way binding for inputs
- [ ] `click:` — click event handler
- [ ] `visible:` — show/hide (keeps in DOM)
- [ ] `if:` / `ifnot:` — conditional (removes/adds from DOM)
- [ ] `foreach:` — iterate over array
- [ ] `css:` — conditional CSS classes `{ 'class': condition }`
- [ ] `attr:` — dynamic HTML attributes `{ href: url }`
- [ ] `$data`, `$root`, `$parent`, `$parents[n]`, `$index()` — context variables
- [ ] `$index` is an observable inside `foreach` — must call `$index()` to get number

### Custom Binding Handlers

- [ ] Register on `ko.bindingHandlers.myBindingName`
- [ ] `init` function runs once on first application
- [ ] `update` function runs once on init and on every change
- [ ] Always call `valueAccessor()` (as a function) to get the binding value
- [ ] Use `ko.unwrap(valueAccessor())` for values that may be observable OR plain

### UI Component Architecture

- [ ] Three pillars: JS component + XML config + PHP data provider
- [ ] JS components extend `uiElement` (single) or `uiCollection` (with children)
- [ ] Properties in `defaults.tracks` auto-become KO observables
- [ ] `initialize()` must call `this._super()` and `return this`
- [ ] `initObservable()` — use `.track({})` to register observables manually
- [ ] `links` — two-way sync; `imports` — inbound sync; `exports` — outbound sync
- [ ] XML files: `view/adminhtml/ui_component/*.xml`
- [ ] `dataSource` element's `dataProvider class` = PHP class
- [ ] `dataSource component` = JS module path
- [ ] Data provider `getData()` returns `{ totalRecords: N, items: [...] }` for grids
- [ ] Common components: Listing, Form, Column, Filter (Filters), Pager, MassAction

### Exam Danger Zones

- [ ] `var config = { config: { mixins: ... } }` — double nesting!
- [ ] Observable read: `this.obs()` not `this.obs`
- [ ] Observable write: `this.obs('val')` not `this.obs = 'val'`
- [ ] `_super()` in all mixin overrides, especially `initialize`
- [ ] `ko.computed(fn, this)` — don't forget the `this` context
- [ ] `$index()` not `$index` in foreach templates
- [ ] Mixin returns `function(Target){ return Target.extend({...}); }` — two-level return
- [ ] Enable mixin with `true`, disable with `false` in requirejs-config.js

