## 10. Tricky Edge Cases & Gotchas

### Gotcha 1: JSON Quoting in `data-mage-init`

```html
<!-- CORRECT: outer single quotes, inner double quotes -->
<div data-mage-init='{"Vendor_Module/js/widget": {"option": "value"}}'></div>

<!-- WRONG: double quotes outside will break HTML attribute -->
<div data-mage-init="{"Vendor_Module/js/widget": {"option": "value"}}"></div>

<!-- Also valid: HTML entities for inner quotes (avoid if possible) -->
<div data-mage-init="{&quot;Vendor_Module/js/widget&quot;: {}}"></div>
```

- **Exam focus:** `data-mage-init` attribute uses **single quotes** as the HTML attribute delimiter with standard JSON (double quotes) inside.

### Gotcha 2: Multiple Widgets on One Element

```html
<!-- Both widgets initialize on the SAME element -->
<div data-mage-init='{
    "Vendor_Module/js/widgetA": {"optA": "val1"},
    "Vendor_Module/js/widgetB": {"optB": "val2"}
}'></div>
```

### Gotcha 3: `x-magento-init` for Dynamic Content

```javascript
// When you inject new HTML via AJAX, trigger re-processing:
$.ajax({
    url: "/my/endpoint",
    success: function (html) {
        var $container = $("#dynamic-container");
        $container.html(html);

        // Re-apply all data-mage-init and x-magento-init within new content
        $container.trigger("contentUpdated");
    }
});
```

```html
<!-- The x-magento-init inside AJAX response will be processed after contentUpdated -->
<div class="dynamic-widget"></div>
<script type="text/x-magento-init">
{
    ".dynamic-widget": {
        "Vendor_Module/js/widget": {}
    }
}
</script>
```

- **Exam focus:** Firing `contentUpdated` on the parent container triggers Magento to re-scan and apply widget bindings from `x-magento-init` blocks within the new content.

### Gotcha 4: Translation Key Case Sensitivity

```javascript
// These are DIFFERENT keys in js-translation.json:
$.mage.__("Add to Cart");   // Key: "Add to Cart"
$.mage.__("add to cart");   // Key: "add to cart" -- WON'T match above!
$.mage.__("ADD TO CART");   // Key: "ADD TO CART" -- different again
```

- **Exam focus:** JS translation keys are **case-sensitive**. The string passed to `$.mage.__()` must **exactly match** the key in `js-translation.json`.

### Gotcha 5: Missing vs Empty Translation

```json
// js-translation.json
{
    "Cancel": "",
    "Save": "Enregistrer"
}
```

```javascript
$.mage.__("Cancel");        // Returns "Cancel" (original) — empty value treated as missing
$.mage.__("Save");          // Returns "Enregistrer"
$.mage.__("Delete");        // Returns "Delete" (original) — key not in JSON at all
```

### Gotcha 6: RequireJS Path Must Match `requirejs-config.js`

```javascript
// requirejs-config.js
var config = {
    map: {
        "*": {
            "greetingWidget": "Vendor_Module/js/greeting-widget"
        }
    }
};
```

```html
<!-- Using the alias in data-mage-init -->
<div data-mage-init='{"greetingWidget": {"name": "World"}}'></div>

<!-- Or the full path (always works without requirejs-config.js alias) -->
<div data-mage-init='{"Vendor_Module/js/greeting-widget": {"name": "World"}}'></div>
```

### Gotcha 7: `_create` vs `_init` Event Binding Duplication

```javascript
$.widget("mage.badWidget", {

    // WRONG: binding in _init causes duplicate listeners on re-init
    _init: function () {
        this._on(this.element, {
            "click": this._handleClick  // Bound again on every re-init!
        });
    }
});

$.widget("mage.goodWidget", {

    // CORRECT: binding in _create = only once
    _create: function () {
        this._on(this.element, {
            "click": this._handleClick  // Bound exactly once
        });
    },

    _init: function () {
        // Only rendering/state updates here
        this._render();
    }
});
```

- **Exam focus:** Always bind events in `_create`. Using `this._on()` (not `.on()`) is preferred because `_on()` automatically cleans up bindings when the widget is destroyed.

### Gotcha 8: `this._on()` vs `$(el).on()`

| | `this._on(element, handlers)` | `$(el).on(event, handler)` |
|---|---|---|
| Auto-cleanup on `_destroy` | **Yes** | No (memory leak risk) |
| Binds context (`this`) | **Automatic** | Manual `.bind(this)` needed |
| Event delegation | Supported | Supported |
| Preferred in widgets | **Yes** | Avoid |

