## Quick-Reference Checklist

### jQuery Widget Pattern
- [ ] Widget defined with `$.widget("namespace.name", { options, _create, _init, methods })`
- [ ] `namespace.name` format: `mage.widgetName` (core) or `vendorName.widgetName` (custom)
- [ ] `options: {}` holds default configuration, overridable at initialization time
- [ ] **`_create` runs exactly ONCE** — use for event binding and one-time setup
- [ ] **`_init` runs on creation AND every re-initialization** — use for rendering/state
- [ ] Always call `this._super(key, value)` in `_setOption` before custom logic
- [ ] Use `this._on()` not `.on()` for auto-cleanup on widget destroy
- [ ] Public methods: no underscore prefix; Private methods: `_underscore` prefix (convention)
- [ ] Widget instance stored in `.data("namespaceWidgetname")` (camelCase)
- [ ] Call public methods: `$(el).widgetName("methodName", args)` or via `.data()` instance

### Widget Initialization
- [ ] `data-mage-init` — HTML attribute on target element; `this.element` = that element
- [ ] `x-magento-init` — `<script type="text/x-magento-init">` with CSS selector
- [ ] Both accept JSON: `{"requirejs/path": {"option": "value"}}`
- [ ] `data-mage-init` uses **single quotes** as outer HTML attribute delimiter
- [ ] `x-magento-init` with `"*"` selector: no DOM element binding (pure JS component)
- [ ] Multiple widgets on one element: multiple keys in the JSON object
- [ ] Dynamic/AJAX content: use `x-magento-init` + fire `contentUpdated` event on container
- [ ] Both processed by `mage/mage.js` (`mage/apply/main` for `data-mage-init`, `mage/apply/scripts` for `x-magento-init`)

### JS Translation
- [ ] `$.mage.__("string")` = `$t("string")` (from `mage/translate`) — functionally identical
- [ ] Both read from **`js-translation.json`** (flat JSON key-value file in `pub/static/`)
- [ ] Missing key or empty string value → returns **original string** (no error)
- [ ] Translation keys are **case-sensitive** — must exactly match what was passed to `$t()`
- [ ] Dynamic values use `%1` placeholder: `$t("Hello %1").replace("%1", name)`

### `js-translation.json` & SCD
- [ ] Generated during **`bin/magento setup:static-content:deploy`** (SCD)
- [ ] Located at `pub/static/{area}/{vendor}/{theme}/{locale}/js-translation.json`
- [ ] Changes to CSV files require **re-running SCD** to update the JSON
- [ ] Loaded in page via `Magento_Translation` module's head block

### Collecting Phrases
- [ ] Command: `bin/magento i18n:collect-phrases`
- [ ] `--magento` flag sets scope to entire Magento root and enables contextual (module-aware) output
- [ ] Both modes (with and without `--magento`) scan PHP, PHTML, JS, HTML, and XML files
- [ ] Output goes to module's `i18n/{locale}.csv` file
- [ ] CSV format: `"Original string","Translated string"`

### PHP vs JS Translation Differences
- [ ] PHP `__()` → reads from **in-memory dictionary** (module CSVs → packs → themes → DB, DB wins)
- [ ] JS `$.mage.__()` → reads from **`js-translation.json` flat file**
- [ ] They are **completely independent** systems — DB changes do NOT affect JS translations
- [ ] PHP translations: live (no deploy needed); JS translations: require SCD
- [ ] Both return original string when translation is not found

### Common Exam Traps
- [ ] `_create` vs `_init` — know which runs when and what each should contain
- [ ] `data-mage-init` (attribute, per-element) vs `x-magento-init` (script tag, CSS selector)
- [ ] `--magento` flag on `i18n:collect-phrases` — scans entire Magento root with contextual output (JS is scanned in both modes)
- [ ] JS translation ≠ PHP translation — different storage, different deploy requirements
- [ ] Empty string in `js-translation.json` = treated as missing = returns original
- [ ] Event binding in `_init` = duplicate listeners on re-init = bug
- [ ] `this._on()` auto-cleans on destroy; raw `.on()` does not

