## 5. Ajax in Magento — `mage/storage`

### Why `mage/storage` instead of `$.ajax()`?

| Feature | `$.ajax()` | `mage/storage` |
|---|---|---|
| REST endpoint support | Manual URL construction | Uses `mage/url` `urlBuilder.build()` automatically |
| Content-Type default | None | `application/json` |
| jQuery global AJAX events | Must set manually | Defaults `global: true` |
| Convenience | Verbose | Cleaner API for REST calls |

> **Important:** `mage/storage` does **NOT** automatically inject auth tokens or session headers. It is a thin wrapper around `$.ajax()` with sensible defaults (`contentType: 'application/json'`, `global: true`) and automatic URL building via `mage/url`. Frontend REST API authentication is handled by PHP session cookies sent automatically by the browser — no explicit `Authorization` header is needed for storefront AJAX calls.

### `mage/storage` API

```javascript
define([
    'mage/storage'
], function (storage) {
    'use strict';

    // GET request — global defaults to true, contentType to 'application/json'
    storage.get(url, global, contentType, headers);

    // POST request — also accepts async (6th param, defaults true)
    storage.post(url, data, global, contentType, headers, async);

    // PUT request
    storage.put(url, data, global, contentType, headers);

    // DELETE request
    storage.delete(url, global, contentType, headers);
});
```

### Return Value — jQuery Deferred

Every `mage/storage` method returns a **jQuery Deferred/Promise**:

```javascript
define([
    'mage/storage'
], function (storage) {
    'use strict';

    return {
        fetchData: function (url) {
            return storage.get(url)
                .done(function (response) {
                    // Success handler
                    console.log('Data received:', response);
                })
                .fail(function (xhr, status, error) {
                    // Error handler
                    console.error('Request failed:', error);
                })
                .always(function () {
                    // Always runs
                    console.log('Request complete');
                });
        }
    };
});
```

### Building REST URLs with `mage/url`

```javascript
define([
    'mage/storage',
    'mage/url'
], function (storage, urlBuilder) {
    'use strict';

    return {
        getCartItems: function () {
            // Builds: https://yourstore.com/rest/V1/carts/mine/items
            var url = urlBuilder.build('rest/V1/carts/mine/items');

            return storage.get(url);
        }
    };
});
```

### Authentication on the Frontend

Frontend REST API calls from the storefront are authenticated via **PHP session cookies** — the browser sends these automatically with every AJAX request. No explicit `Authorization: Bearer` header is needed.

```
Logged-in customer request:
  - PHP session cookie authenticates the customer automatically
  - URL pattern: /rest/V1/carts/mine/items (session identifies the customer)

Guest request:
  - Uses a masked cart ID in the URL path
  - URL pattern: /rest/V1/guest-carts/:maskedCartId/items
  - The masked ID is available via window.checkoutConfig or quote model
```

- **Exam focus:** `mage/storage` is a convenience wrapper — it does NOT inject auth tokens. Frontend REST API auth relies on session cookies (automatic) and URL-based cart identification (guest masked IDs).

### Complete REST API Example

```javascript
define([
    'mage/storage',
    'Magento_Checkout/js/model/url-builder',
    'Magento_Customer/js/model/customer'
], function (storage, checkoutUrlBuilder, customer) {
    'use strict';

    return {
        /**
         * Fetch current cart items
         * @returns {jQuery.Deferred}
         */
        getCartItems: function () {
            var url;

            if (customer.isLoggedIn()) {
                // Authenticated customer cart
                url = checkoutUrlBuilder.createUrl('/carts/mine/items', {});
            } else {
                // Guest cart — requires quote mask ID
                var quoteId = window.checkoutConfig.quoteData.entity_id;
                url = checkoutUrlBuilder.createUrl(
                    '/guest-carts/:cartId/items',
                    { cartId: quoteId }
                );
            }

            return storage.get(url, false)
                .done(function (items) {
                    console.log('Cart items:', items);
                })
                .fail(function (response) {
                    console.error('Failed to load cart items', response);
                });
        }
    };
});
```

