## Quick-Reference Checklist

### AMD Fundamentals
- [ ] `define([deps], factory)` — creates a reusable module with exports
- [ ] `require([deps], callback)` — consumes modules without creating exports
- [ ] Dependency array positions **must match** factory argument positions
- [ ] `'use strict'` is **required** by Magento coding standards inside every factory
- [ ] `requirejs-config.js` lives in `view/frontend/` or `view/adminhtml/`
- [ ] `requirejs-config.js` supports: `map`, `paths`, `shim`, `config.mixins`

### Module Isolation
- [ ] Every AMD factory runs in its own function scope — no global leakage
- [ ] Variables inside `define()` are **not** accessible from outside
- [ ] Only the `return` value is shared — expose only what is needed

### Dependency Injection
- [ ] Declare every dependency in the array — **never** assume a module is already loaded
- [ ] Never rely on load order between separate `require()` calls
- [ ] Argument count should equal dependency array length

### Common Magento Modules
- [ ] `jquery` → `$` — DOM, events, AJAX base
- [ ] `underscore` → `_` — functional utilities
- [ ] `ko` → `ko` — Knockout.js MVVM
- [ ] `mage/storage` — REST API AJAX with automatic auth headers
- [ ] `mage/url` / `mage/translate` → `urlBuilder` / `$t`
- [ ] `mage/utils/wrapper` — wraps functions non-destructively (use for mixins)
- [ ] `Magento_Customer/js/model/customer` — `customer.isLoggedIn()` (KO observable)
- [ ] `Magento_Checkout/js/model/quote` — `quote.totals()`, `quote.shippingAddress()` (KO observables)
- [ ] KO observables are **functions** — must be called with `()` to get value

### mage/storage AJAX
- [ ] `storage.get(url)` — HTTP GET
- [ ] `storage.post(url, data)` — HTTP POST
- [ ] `storage.put(url, data)` — HTTP PUT
- [ ] `storage.delete(url)` — HTTP DELETE
- [ ] Returns **jQuery Deferred** — chain `.done()`, `.fail()`, `.always()`
- [ ] Does NOT auto-inject auth tokens — frontend REST API uses session cookies (automatic)
- [ ] Use `mage/url` or `Magento_Checkout/js/model/url-builder` to construct URLs

### JS Performance & Build
- [ ] Developer mode: individual file requests, no bundling
- [ ] Production mode: minification enabled, bundling available
- [ ] `setup:static-content:deploy -f en_US` deploys and minifies static assets
- [ ] **RequireJS bundling** combines AMD modules into fewer HTTP requests
- [ ] **Grunt** is used for theme development: LESS compilation, watching, redeployment
- [ ] Grunt theme must be registered in `dev/tools/grunt/configs/themes.js`
- [ ] `grunt less:<theme>`, `grunt watch`, `grunt exec:<theme>`, `grunt clean:<theme>`

### Tricky / Pitfalls
- [ ] RequireJS is **async** — never assume load order without explicit dependencies
- [ ] **Circular dependencies** = silent failure; one module receives `{}` (empty object)
- [ ] Fix circular deps: extract shared module, or use lazy `require()` inside function
- [ ] Always include `mage/translate` explicitly — `$t('string')` is the preferred pattern
- [ ] `$.mage.__()` works but is fragile — use `mage/translate` → `$t` instead
- [ ] Argument count mismatch = last deps are `undefined` — match array length exactly
- [ ] KO observables without `()` return the function, not the value

### Hands-On Verification
- [ ] AMD module: `define()` with `mage/storage`, `mage/url`, `mage/translate`
- [ ] `storage.get()` call against `/rest/V1/carts/mine/items`
- [ ] Verify in Network tab: XHR request appears, status 200, JSON response
- [ ] Verify auth header automatically added to logged-in customer request
- [ ] No global variables: confirm no new properties on `window` object
